  "findings": [
    "Actual loops are unrolled differently: AVX2 split32/group64 ranks; AVX512 split64/group128. Normalize all counts/resource cycles by these ranks. All four bodies are call-free and stack-free. No hardware gather, staged scratch or additional per-row field request hides in grouped R+U.",
    "Normalized vector work is identical within each ISA: two narrow R/U loads, widened u32 addition, u64 extensions/extraction and checksum additions. Both issue4 explicit payload bytes/rank. Grouped has fewer total instructions and address-MOV/AND/LEA sites per rank, and fewer loop-carried lo/hi checksum writes; temporary checksum reassociation remains genuine work.",
    "Split loads progress through two R/U planes; grouped loads16-row R/U chunks from one interleaved stream. Byte footprints/counts match logically; codegen alone does not establish actual lines fetched, resident sets, hit/miss service or prefetch behavior.",
    "LLVM21 accepts -mcpu=znver5 for both instruction sets but scheduling resources are named Zn4*. Modeled reciprocal resource throughput/rank is equal: .5 cycles AVX2 and.3125 AVX512. Finite1000-loop simulation gives grouped approximately0.33% lower cycles/rank in AVX2 and3.24% higher in AVX512. No modeled gap comparable with the root-reported approximately18% large-set grouped penalty.",
    "Emitted compute differences and this inherited model do not provide a compelling explanation for that large-set gap. Hot256 approximately level and size-dependent separation keep memory geometry/whole-machine behavior unresolved. This is an inference about which question remains, not a specific measured memory cause or exclusion of every unmodeled compute effect."
  ],
  "model_limits": [
    "Scheduling diagnostic only; not measured cycles, peak throughput or hardware causality. Branch prediction/frontend fetch, caches/prefetchers, physical addresses, TLBs, outstanding requests, clock and operating interference not resolved.",
    "MCA assumes scheduled repeating instruction streams and abstract load service. BRT is a resource bound; finite cycles also reflect dependencies. Different unroll counts normalized; setup, tail and final reduction excluded, so no full-cell timing prediction.",
    "The znver5 selection uses inherited Zn4 resource names and instruction data; no assertion the model captures the actual Zen5 SIMD implementation or all resource capacities. No exact hardware gain/loss ratio or tuning recommendation from the model alone."
  ],
  "commands": "taskset -c2 llvm-mca-21 -mtriple=x86_64 -mcpu=znver5 -iterations=1000 -instruction-info -resource-pressure <exact .mca.s>; individual argument arrays and stdout/stderr hashes in extracts.json."
